{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1454643-what-if-the-god-machines-is-just-playing","id":1454643,"title":"What if the God-Machines is just... playing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-10T00:32:55-07:00","id":1454643,"title":"What if the God-Machines is just... playing?","content":"Okay so, at first I didn't believed it warranted it's own thread, but here I am...<br /> <br /> basically, it game from a discussion about the French translation of Guide to the Night and Half-Damned where it drifted to the God Machine playfully. And then it hit me...<br /> <br /> What if it was all a game, for the God-Machine that is ? What if it allows Angels to fall or go exile not out of malice but because it wants to play? That it deliberately created rules to instantly erase and expunge all traces of the Covers used by his Angels when they fall, to better it up ,<br /> <br /> Would it do that to kept iself sharp? To protect himself from boredom? To repurpose stuff it knows is now unnecessary but just doesn't want to destroy outright or recycle imediately? <br /> <br /> What would it entail for the players and the world at large, if the God-Machine was really just trying to play and had no malice, no ill-will toward its wayward children? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T12:00:25-07:00","id":1454655,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if that makes it more or less fuckwad-y.<br /> <br /> Either way, it's a entity of immense power and metaphysical authority abusing basically everything in the world. Whether those ends are self-preservation, &quot;for our own good&quot;, or play-which is worse or better is left to the tastes of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T20:43:34-07:00","id":1454670,"title":"","content":"The span and scope of things it is trying to manipulate and the reasons therefor are so out-there that there's basically no extra nuance added in the assumption that an edifice as corrupt and obfuscated as the God-Machine is using the Unchained and the Abandoned as an idle diversion rather than that it's a whole chaotic mess eating itself due to imperfect information and willful bad-action.<br /> <br /> The easiest thematic connective tissue between the Machine and vampires is in its <a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/620768355438198784/unauthorized-water\" target=\"_blank\">subversion of existing systems to suit its designs</a>. The most direct tie between the Machine and even its most left-alone fugitives is the fact that they are wasted resources (angels who are disconnected from automatic awareness of their duties) that collect and engineer other <a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/633044700166766592\" target=\"_blank\">wasted resources</a> (Aether that has been transformed from Essence to produce an output). The most straightforward way to explain the apparent total disconnect from reality that seems to occasionally inform the Machine's decision-making process is a combination of good old-fashioned &quot;garbage in, garbage out&quot; and the fact that <a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/650627976084504576/maxofs2d-tsunderebot-dexer-von-dexer\" target=\"_blank\">it does not look at reality like a person does</a>.<br /> <br /> It makes no appreciable difference if the Machine is playing a perverse and malicious game with humanity or merely acting on perverse and malicious biases in its data-gathering methods. It does not have anybody else's best interests in mind, and that makes a being of its scope and power <i>de facto</i> monstrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T09:00:37-07:00","id":1456073,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the long delay in that answer... it seems this thread displeased the God-Machine since my computer's alimentation died on me and I had to have it remplaced, which was... a whole adventure, in its own way.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Machine is inherently an absolute horror... but I feel that there are too many inconsistencies in the way it deals with the Covers of his former Angels. It's something I've never been able to understand : why does it doesn't have a database of all his Covers? Sure, it's more probably good old fashioned not caring one bit about it because the Demons are so small that they aren't a threat worth considering between being some damned resources which can be reused. But I still find it strange, because even if they are a small hindrance, they are still bothering him somewhat. <br /> <br /> There has to be a reason for it, surely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T10:48:25-07:00","id":1456079,"title":"","content":"Considering the God Machine\u2019s ties to the cosmic horror genre\u2026 that way lies madness.<br /> <br /> Personally, I also can\u2019t stand there being an unknowable reason (or none at all), especially as a ST, but it\u2019s baked into the whole concept of the GM quite specifically. So if there is a Reason, it\u2019s going to be unique to each chronicle.<br /> <br /> That said, there\u2019s a lot of classic horror themes around it\u2019s motive being \u201cto play\u201d. The idea of something having vast power and no responsibility is pretty abhorrent to many cultures; compounded by being completely at the whim of something capricious; and the terrible responsibility of being the only person who can try keeping this omnipotent being on the rails. There\u2019s a lot of fiction about wealthy elites, the fae, and children with super powers that hit that same kind of horror. And it there are some cosmic horror stories that have built up to that realization as well.<br /> <br /> So, it could work as a motive in your personal chronicles. And if it helps you pull your plot together to have a defined motive (it certainly does for me), then go for it. I believe the cannon answers, and most storytellers\u2019 approach, though, will be \u201cthe GM has no understandable motive - but its human cultists do\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 08-03-2021, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T13:00:27-07:00","id":1456087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1454643-what-if-the-god-machines-is-just-playing?p=1456073#post1456073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the long delay in that answer... it seems this thread displeased the God-Machine since my computer's alimentation died on me and I had to have it remplaced, which was... a whole adventure, in its own way.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Machine is inherently an absolute horror... but I feel that there are too many inconsistencies in the way it deals with the Covers of his former Angels. It's something I've never been able to understand : why does it doesn't have a database of all his Covers? Sure, it's more probably good old fashioned not caring one bit about it because the Demons are so small that they aren't a threat worth considering between being some damned resources which can be reused. But I still find it strange, because even if they are a small hindrance, they are still bothering him somewhat. <br /> <br /> There has to be a reason for it, surely.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably has a database containing all Covers, but during the Fall demons probably disconnects all of the infrastructures concerning their Covers and infos about it from the GM","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T20:44:47-07:00","id":1456102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1454643-what-if-the-god-machines-is-just-playing?p=1456073#post1456073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the Machine is inherently an absolute horror... but I feel that there are too many inconsistencies in the way it deals with the Covers of his former Angels. It's something I've never been able to understand : why does it doesn't have a database of all his Covers? Sure, it's more probably good old fashioned not caring one bit about it because the Demons are so small that they aren't a threat worth considering between being some damned resources which can be reused. But I still find it strange, because even if they are a small hindrance, they are still bothering him somewhat.<br /> <br /> There has to be a reason for it, surely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basic tradecraft says to:<br /> 1. Not keep rigorous notes on all the clandestine and/or wildly illegal shit you're getting up to, because if that information exists in concrete form then someone can get it without having to get it the hard way.<br /> 2. Not keep that information all in one place if it <i>does</i> exist in concrete form, because providing an easy way to get it all and providing a <i>very</i> easy way to get it all are two very different things.<br /> 3. Burn after reading. The Unchained have perfect memories for a reason. Which brings me to\u2026<br /> <br /> The basics of how the God-Machine operates include:<br /> 1. It lives in all its work, i.e. its angels <i>are</i> the database for their Cover-equivalent Infrastructure until they Fall, and pre-made redundancies in this data storage are a liability, as outlined above.<br /> 2. It is decentralized to the point where it can be at war with itself <i>before</i> demonic involvement steps it, i.e. it's made up of disconnected cells and the right hand doesn't know what the left is doing.<br /> 3. It is a temporal being subject to the constraints of entropy, at least as far as the forms it uses to interact with the world are concerned, i.e. the occult physics it uses to work miracles require components and circumstances that must be contrived or lucked into, and turning the basement of a disused library and some impressionable grad students into a surveillance operation for every demon in town means it can't use those things for something else without a hard pivot and it'd be stretching them thin to use them that way without yet more support structures. If you wish to make an apple pie from scratch, you must first invent the universe. And on that note\u2026<br /> <br /> It's not so much that demons are a minor nuisance as it is that they're as usable as everything else is to the Machine, and energy they can be tricked into spending on the Machine's interests is energy it's not spending itself. Why commission Elimination Infrastructure to tear down that old facility when you can just lure some Saboteurs into blowing it up? Why build a cult when you can subvert a Tempter's network? Why send a fresh Analyst to look into a weird problem when you can blackmail an Inquisitor into doing it for less? The Principle of Least Action is part of the Machine's SOP for good reason, and the fact that it's lacking enough in oversight to routinely produce demons combined with the fact that it's canny enough to make them think more of those Falls were pushed than they were is a prime demonstration of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T08:19:21-07:00","id":1456123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1454643-what-if-the-god-machines-is-just-playing?p=1456102#post1456102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basic tradecraft says to:<br /> 1. Not keep rigorous notes on all the clandestine and/or wildly illegal shit you're getting up to, because if that information exists in concrete form then someone can get it without having to get it the hard way.<br /> 2. Not keep that information all in one place if it <i>does</i> exist in concrete form, because providing an easy way to get it all and providing a <i>very</i> easy way to get it all are two very different things.<br /> 3. Burn after reading. The Unchained have perfect memories for a reason. Which brings me to\u2026<br /> <br /> The basics of how the God-Machine operates include:<br /> 1. It lives in all its work, i.e. its angels <i>are</i> the database for their Cover-equivalent Infrastructure until they Fall, and pre-made redundancies in this data storage are a liability, as outlined above.<br /> 2. It is decentralized to the point where it can be at war with itself <i>before</i> demonic involvement steps it, i.e. it's made up of disconnected cells and the right hand doesn't know what the left is doing.<br /> 3. It is a temporal being subject to the constraints of entropy, at least as far as the forms it uses to interact with the world are concerned, i.e. the occult physics it uses to work miracles require components and circumstances that must be contrived or lucked into, and turning the basement of a disused library and some impressionable grad students into a surveillance operation for every demon in town means it can't use those things for something else without a hard pivot and it'd be stretching them thin to use them that way without yet more support structures. If you wish to make an apple pie from scratch, you must first invent the universe. And on that note\u2026<br /> <br /> It's not so much that demons are a minor nuisance as it is that they're as usable as everything else is to the Machine, and energy they can be tricked into spending on the Machine's interests is energy it's not spending itself. Why commission Elimination Infrastructure to tear down that old facility when you can just lure some Saboteurs into blowing it up? Why build a cult when you can subvert a Tempter's network? Why send a fresh Analyst to look into a weird problem when you can blackmail an Inquisitor into doing it for less? The Principle of Least Action is part of the Machine's SOP for good reason, and the fact that it's lacking enough in oversight to routinely produce demons combined with the fact that it's canny enough to make them think more of those Falls were pushed than they were is a prime demonstration of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it makes sense even if I never considered the possbility that Demons are liable to unwittingly do what the Machine would want. At the very least, the idea that each Angel is basically is sole database and at the same time the data and output of his Cover makes perfect sense, it certainly helps me deal with something which has always kind of bothered me in the Fall of Angels.<br /> <br /> But would it be a glitch of his part or a feature that Angels can Fall then ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T20:55:53-07:00","id":1456161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1454643-what-if-the-god-machines-is-just-playing?p=1456123#post1456123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But would it be a glitch of his part or a feature that Angels can Fall then ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's part of the way the world works. Demon is distinguished from the other two gamelines with godlike beings who command magical servitors by the fact that angels' &quot;native plane&quot; is the one where the others consistently drift out of alignment with their creators. As long as there's a force of destiny defining a path of least resistance, there's going to be gears that catch and cars that veer off course, especially in the material world.<br /> <br /> The Machine, despite being blind to many of its flaws by the nature of its perceptions, is no stranger to the fact that the Fall happens, and may prepare for individual instances of the phenomenon, be it to engineer a particular catalyst or steer a would-be demon away from the precipice. It's hard to say whether the Fall is a feature or a bug without knowing what exactly the Machine <i>is</i>, but as a system that at least makes a good show of self-awareness, its processes include methods of managing Falls or using Falls to manage other problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}